# Runbook sources and matching reference

Authoritative reference for the `on-call-{{ROTATION}}` skill. Update this file when
runbooks move. The workflow reads from here so it stays stable.

## Confluence access

- **Site:** `commercetools.atlassian.net`
- **cloudId:** `{{CLOUD_ID}}`
- If a call fails with an auth error, refresh with `getAccessibleAtlassianResources`.

## Index pages

Enumerate every run with `getConfluencePageDescendants` (`depth: 2`, generous
`limit`). Never body-fetch these. They time out.

{{RUNBOOK_INDEXES_DETAIL}}

## Standing dashboards

Golden signals dashboards. Surface the one for the incident service. Set
`var-cloud` and the time range to the incident.

{{DASHBOARDS}}

## Environments

The environment maps to a single cloud id, used in three places. The dashboard
`var-cloud`, the Prometheus datasource UID, and the LogScale `?account`.

{{ENV_TABLE}}

Refresh ids with `grafana_list_datasources(type=prometheus)` if one looks stale.

## Dependencies and upstream status

Decide "is it us or upstream?" and surface the relevant status page. Choose by the
cloud of the environment and by the dependency.

- AWS envs. https://health.aws.amazon.com/health/status
- GCP envs. https://status.cloud.google.com
{{DEPENDENCIES}}

## Service repositories

For recent-changes correlation, prefer the `Github repo` field in the matched
runbook. Use this map as the fallback. All under the `commercetools` org.

{{SERVICE_REPOS}}

## Runbook taxonomy

- **`Diagnostic: <Service> <Signal>`** are the symptom entry points. Titles track
  alert names.
- **`Action: <Remediation>`** are the fixes a Diagnostic links to.
- Legacy free-form titles. Match on keywords when the modern naming is absent.

Skip category container pages and reference docs.

## Service vocabulary

{{SERVICE_VOCAB}}

## Signal vocabulary

| Signal | Triggers in the symptom |
|---|---|
| Elevated Error Rate | error rate, 5xx, 500s, failing requests |
| Elevated Latency | latency, slow, p95, timeouts |
| Nodejs Event Loop Lag | event loop, lag, CPU pegged |
| Pod Elevated Number Of Restarts | restarts, crashloop |
| Memory Pressure | memory, OOM, OOMKilled |
| 502 / load balancer | 502, bad gateway |

## What to extract when summarizing a runbook

- Metadata. Owner, Service, Github repo, Approximate Runtime, Prerequisites.
- The standing dashboard for the service plus any dashboard linked in the steps.
- Humio / LogScale queries. Link and raw text.
- Linked `Action:` runbooks and sibling `Diagnostic:` pages.
